553	\label{thm:mi_decomp}
554	Let $X$ be a random input window, $E \in \{1,\ldots,K\}$ the expert assignment produced by any deterministic router, $S = (X - M)/\Sigma$ the RevIN-normalized shape. \emph{(i) Exact decomposition:} $I(X;E) - I(S;E) = I(M,\Sigma;E\mid S) \geq 0$. \emph{(ii) Quantitative bound (no independence assumption):} $I(X;E) - I(S;E) \geq I(M,\Sigma;E) - I(M,\Sigma;S)$, with $\varepsilon := I(M,\Sigma;S) \geq 0$ capturing residual leakage of stripped statistics through the shape; equality iff $(M,\Sigma) \perp\!\!\!\perp S \mid E$.
