501	\textbf{Rescue-baseline sweep.} To rule out that the collapse is merely under-tuned, we sweep five standard MoE rescue families (Switch load-balance~\citep{fedus2022switch}, ST-MoE z-loss~\citep{zoph2022stmoe}, entropy regularization, ReMoE ReLU routing~\citep{wang2025remoe}, and expert-choice routing~\citep{zhou2022expertchoice}) across eleven new rescue configurations plus the load-balance baseline already in Table~\ref{tab:adamix} ($12$ configurations total $\times$ 6 datasets $\times$ 2 freeze levels $\times$ 5 seeds $= 720$ run-cells) (Table~\ref{tab:rescue}, Appendix~\ref{app:rescue_details}). The best rescue (z-loss $c_z{=}0.01$) reduces MSE by only $10.9\%$, still $2.7{\times}$ worse than RR-MoA. Excessive balancing ($\alpha{=}10.0$) actively hurts MSE ($+67.7\%$). This is consistent with Observation~\ref{thm:mi_decomp}(ii): when routing information is structurally absent from the hidden states, none of the standard rescue mechanisms we tested can compensate.
502	
503	\textbf{The principle is architecture-agnostic.} Three router-level controls validate that any router reading raw input suffices. \textbf{SR-MoA} (Figure~\ref{fig:srmoa_arch}; cf.~\citealp{lv2025aoe,liu2026routingfree,cheng2025ermoe}) drops the external router: each expert has its own sigmoid gate $\sigma_k(\mathbf{X}_\mathrm{raw})$. It \emph{outperforms} RR-MoA by $13$--$42\%$ across all 6 datasets ($252$-run, six-backbone grid; Table~\ref{tab:self_routed}) and replicates the Frozen Paradox ($4/6$). Gating the same architecture on hidden states degrades by $+87$--$768\%$ ($p{=}0.016$); on Timer-XL the same comparison yields only $+4$--$9\%$, $15$--$100{\times}$ smaller, consistent with normalization being the cause. \textbf{AdaMix-Raw} (Appendix~\ref{app:adamix_details}) swaps the hidden-state router for raw input and recovers entropy to $1.41$--$1.57$ and MSE by $41$--$88\%$ on all 12 cells. \textbf{Residual-IA\textsuperscript{+}} (Appendix~\ref{app:gate_pathology}, Figure~\ref{fig:residual_ia_arch}) extends the principle to the expert level via a shared NLinear raw branch + gated backbone residual. Table~\ref{tab:causal_controls} summarizes all eight controls.
